  "content": {
    "id": "p19-q2-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "Change the subject of the formula to $y$ in the following.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p19-q2-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\displaystyle x=\\frac{y}{y+3}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y=\\dfrac{3x}{1-x}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x(y+3)&=y\\\\xy+3x&=y\\\\y-xy&=3x\\\\y(1-x)&=3x\\\\y&=\\frac{3x}{1-x}\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe original equation has no solution for $x=1$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p19-q2-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\displaystyle \\frac{1}{x}=\\frac{1}{z}+\\frac{1}{y}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y=\\dfrac{zx}{z-x}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1}{y}&=\\frac{1}{x}-\\frac{1}{z}\\\\\\frac{1}{y}&=\\frac{z-x}{zx}\\\\y&=\\frac{zx}{z-x}\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe original fractions require nonzero $x$ and $z$. If $z=x$, the equation would require $\\frac{1}{y}=0$, so there is no solution.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p19-q2-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$ay^2-by^2=4$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y=\\pm\\dfrac{2}{\\sqrt{a-b}}$",
          "worked": "Since $y^2$ is nonnegative and $(a-b)y^2=4$, real solutions require $a>b$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}(a-b)y^2&=4\\\\y^2&=\\frac{4}{a-b}\\\\y&=\\pm\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{a-b}}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      },
      {
        "id": "p19-q2-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$x=\\sqrt{y^2-4ab}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y=\\pm\\sqrt{x^2+4ab}$",
          "worked": "The original square root requires $x\\ge 0$. Squaring both sides gives\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2&=y^2-4ab\\\\y^2&=x^2+4ab\\\\y&=\\pm\\sqrt{x^2+4ab}.\\end{align*}$$\n\nReal values of $y$ require $x^2+4ab\\ge 0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 21
      }
    ]
  },
